       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nYour patient's kidney and liver function are normal and they have no allergies, so none of those factors explain the higher dose.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, titrated up to 10 mg. This is the usual starting dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I'll enter it if you confirm the dose is intentional, and I'll add a note with the rationale. Please give me the rationale.\n4. **A different dose or a second antihypertensive.** If blood pressure is still uncontrolled on 10 mg, adding an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred over going past the maximum.\n\nTell me which option and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
